## Lore

Nobody knows where the Armored Slayer comes from. At first sight it looks
like a huge armored soldier, or something bred by the bio-wizards of
Atlantis: a hunched, barrel-chested hulk of plates, spikes and knotted
bone, with stumpy legs, heavy arms, and hands whose two or three fingers
are really blades, jagged metal or gun barrels fixed in place. Six long
tentacles hang where a mouth should be.

The hulk is a shell. The real creature is a pale red mass like an
oversized brain, with two yellow eyes on short stalks and those six
tentacles, about the size of a human torso. Much as a hermit crab borrows
a shell, it builds a body out of scrap metal, stone, wood and bone, glued
and coated with a grey resin it secretes, and steers it through hair-thin
tendrils helped along by telekinesis. Inside that body it moves with a
speed and grace nothing so heavy should have. Outside it, it can only
crawl.

It eats psychic energy, never flesh, and it hates supernatural beings and
hunts them, which is how it earned its name. That ought to make it
welcome. Instead it is one of the most feared and misunderstood creatures
in North America: it is thoroughly alien, grasps people, speech and law
only up to a point, and acts on instinct and feeling. The Coalition has
killed thousands, and the Slayers have learned to fear the Death''s Head
and to keep away from towns. A few do fall in with humanoid bands that
fight demons and monsters, where they are loyal, cunning in a simple way,
and about as subtle as a bull in a china shop.

## GM Notes

The book heads the Armored Slayer an NPC monster and optional player
character; whether to allow one is left to the G.M. It takes no O.C.C.
and levels on the Dragon experience table.

The sheet stores the armored body: main body 300 M.D.C. (the book prints
300-420, with 300 average and 420 the most the creature can build up to),
P.S. 2D6+22 and Spd 3D6+16. The limbs, the head, the tentacles and the
eyes have their own M.D.C., listed under the natural abilities, and the
organism inside has P.E. x2 M.D.C. of its own.

It favors prey rich in P.P.E. or I.S.P.: demons, dragons, Faerie Folk,
psychics and practitioners of magic. Those of good alignment, and members
of a group it has joined, may be spared, but a teammate who threatens it
or is seen consorting with the enemy is fought to the death.

Size 9-12 feet (2.7 to 3.6 m). Weight 1500 to 4000 pounds (675 to 1800
kg). Life span unknown, thought to be 300-600 years.

Habitat: eastern Canada and the eastern United States and all around
Hudson Bay, usually near large bodies of water, in ruins, forest and
marsh; it avoids mountains and inhabited cities. Occasionally met in
Alberta. Encountered alone, in pairs, or in groups of 3-6.

Allies: Inuit, Cyber-Knights and fellow demon slayers, though few Slayers
keep company outside their own kind. Enemies: demons and evil
supernatural beings first; Coalition soldiers are dangerous and avoided.

The block prints no money and no equipment.
